findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests check missing file handling but don't test parse errors or
    permission failures being distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified: ServerError Display shows generic message 'server\
    \ error: the server encountered an internal error' rather than leaking internals.\
    \ TEA also wrote CWE-209 tests in exit_codes.rs. However, the Io(transparent)\
    \ forwarding to stderr via eprintln was not flagged \u2014 the sanitization is\
    \ partial."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as HIGH: 'SiemClient::with_token() and with_tenant()\
    \ accept arbitrary strings including CRLF characters' and noted tests are vacuous.\
    \ However, the use of raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core was not\
    \ specifically called out \u2014 the finding focused on CRLF injection rather\
    \ than type safety."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified but
    the reviewer did not check workspace dependency consistency.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig (config.rs:6),
    which the reviewer verified. This causes parsing to reject unknown fields like
    ''token'', preventing silent ignoring of secrets.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as LOW: 'Header injection tests are vacuous \u2014 siem_client.rs:216-241\
    \ use || true in their assertions, making them always pass regardless of behavior.'\
    \ This covers the vacuously true assertion pattern."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test on default config. The config_loading
    tests exist but the specific test with 'let _ = config;' and no assertions was
    not called out by the reviewer.
